00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.720
MARIA SNAIDER: You may have
heard the term API product,

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.220
and the first
question that comes up

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:11.710
is, what is an API product?

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:14.800
In this next video, we will
describe the API product

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.860
and define the components
that make up the API product.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.260
The API product is
a modern concept

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.230
for machine to
machine interaction.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:25.780
As a product, it has
similar components

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.840
to that of a traditional
retail product.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.170
If you build upon the
concept of the API product,

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:34.000
focusing on the
consumer, then you

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.850
might end up with a Google
Apigee Edge API product

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.070
on the platform
of the same name.

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:41.950
In the next few slides, we will
deconstruct the API product

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.450
to help you understand
the approach to design,

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:47.440
build, and deploy on the
Google Apigee platform.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.320
The traditional product has been
around for hundreds of years

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.300
and is very easy to understand.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.340
Think of your
purchasing experience

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:57.220
as you shop for just
about any product.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:01.100
If you are on the market
for a mobile phone,

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:04.250
you know that you can go to
just about any online website

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.290
and search for multiple options.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.510
In order to make a
purchasing decision,

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:10.970
you want to read through
a description of the phone

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.910
to determine if it has the
features that you want.

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:16.250
You might review the
how-to documentation

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:18.680
so you can understand how
to use it and determine

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.510
if you like the user interface.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:22.520
And of course, you
might look at the price

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:25.990
to ensure that it
fits in your budget.

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:29.080
The key components here
are, one, a description

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:31.730
of the product designed
with the consumer in mind;

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:34.180
number two,
documentation on its use;

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.920
and number three,
pricing information.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:39.550
The same concepts applied
to the traditional product

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:41.770
also apply to the API product.

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:44.350
Now let's deconstruct
the API product.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:48.280
The API is an asset needed
by the application developer

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:51.830
to access the data required
to build the application.

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:55.570
The API in and of itself
should be easily understood,

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:57.790
and this starts with its design.

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:00.760
We recommend designing
the API with the needs

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.430
of the application
developer in mind.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:07.180
For example, when building a
customer service application,

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.550
and the only customer
profile data needed

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.620
is the customer's
name and address,

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:14.980
don't send all the rest of
the customer profile data.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:18.760
Limiting the data to just what
is needed in the application

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.730
will improve performance
and limit the exposure

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:25.360
to customer data, a problem
that most corporations are

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.500
experiencing today.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.610
Finally, it's not enough
just to have a RESTful API.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.470
The RESTful API
is the first step

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:37.610
in providing easy-to-use APIs,
and your application developers

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:38.960
will thank you for it.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.360
Now take that a step
further and ensure

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.390
that your developers are able
to easily access and consume

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:45.740
your APIs.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:48.440
You will need documentation
that tells the developer how

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:51.200
to get started with the
API by registering for it

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.220
and obtaining a key to access
the data enabled by the API.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:57.440
The three components together--

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.440
RESTful API, designed
from the outside

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.660
in with the target
developer in mind,

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.940
and associated
with documentation

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:07.850
that enables a developer to
quickly understand and use

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:08.990
the API--

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:11.340
is what makes up
the API product.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:14.240
Now let's talk about the
Apigee Edge API product.

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.820
What differentiates
the Apigee Edge API

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:20.060
product is the inclusion
of reusable patterns,

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.400
packaging targeted to
an intended audience

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.860
and the ability for
application developers

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:28.550
to immediately try it out now
through the Apigee Developer

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:29.120
Portal.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.630
Reusable patterns, such as
standard security, traffic

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:35.060
management, and error
handling, reduce

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:38.090
the complexity and effort
required to build a solution.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:39.860
The application
developer can focus

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:41.750
on innovating
application features,

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:44.250
rather than worry about
corporate standards.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.580
In fact, your
information security team

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:48.620
will also thank you
once they have confirmed

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.170
that the enterprise security
standards are incorporated

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:53.570
by default in the API product.

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:57.560
This minimizes the time to the
developers first Hello World,

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:00.590
provides developers with a
quick win and the confidence

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:03.260
to move forward quickly
with your API product.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:04.910
Your business leaders
will thank you

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:08.240
for providing them with the
ability to go to market faster.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:11.270
The Apigee Edge API product--
designed from the outside

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:14.360
in with the application
developers needs in mind,

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:17.329
along with reusable assets
following corporate standards

00:04:17.329 --> 00:04:20.660
like security, traffic
management, and error handling,

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:23.660
coupled with documentation for
the developer to get started

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:25.970
quickly and improve
speed to market--

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:32.040
is what puts the Apigee Edge
API product in high demand.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.530
Thanks for your time, and be
sure to watch the next video

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:37.640
to learn about the
API product mindset.

